What is the DevOps Lifecycle?

The DevOps Lifecycle is a continuous process used to develop, test, deploy, operate, and improve software through automation and continuous feedback.

Unlike the traditional waterfall model, it is a continuous loop, enabling frequent releases and ongoing improvement.

