Real Interview Scenario

Question: A developer pushes code to GitHub. Explain what happens until it's available to users.

Sample Answer:

The developer pushes code to GitHub.
A CI pipeline starts automatically.
The application is built.
Unit tests run.
SonarQube performs code quality checks.
Trivy scans the Docker image for vulnerabilities.
The image is pushed to Azure Container Registry.
Helm deploys the application to AKS.
Azure Monitor and Application Insights track the application's health.
If issues are detected, alerts are sent and feedback is used to improve the next release.
